Synthwave / Retro 1980s: Focus on glowing neon grids, vibrant sunset color palettes, polished chrome surfaces, 
and geometric laser lines.

Create a promotional album cover in a cyberpunk Synthwave and retro 1980s style, featuring a mysterious artist 
wearing dark clothing with glowing neon outlines, standing in a futuristic city at night. Add neon grids, glowing 
skyscrapers, laser lines, a floating chrome sphere, and a giant holographic portal beneath a vibrant sunset blending
pink, purple, orange, and electric blue. Use deep shadows and bright neon lights to create dramatic contrast, with 
reflections on wet pavement and metallic surfaces. Create depth by placing the artist and floating sphere in the 
foreground, futuristic buildings in the middle ground, and faded skyscrapers and mountains in the distance. 
Suggest time and motion through blurred light trails, moving laser beams, swirling energy around the portal, and 
decaying buildings beside modern structures. Maintain unity with a consistent neon color palette while adding variety
through unusual holographic shapes and contrasting textures, including polished chrome, rough concrete, glowing glass,
and subtle vintage film grain. Use an asymmetrical composition, making the artist the main focal point and balancing 
their visual weight with the oversized portal and glowing skyline. Vary the size and detail of objects to establish depth
and scale, creating a distinctive, cinematic, mysterious, and energetic album cover with an authentic 1980s futuristic
atmosphere.

